      "evidence": "At Ethereum block 25526164 and Sonic block 75897805, current RolesAuthority capabilities and complete role histories resolved the sole direct BoringVault enter caller, both chain-specific governance Safes, and all four Accountant role-11 rate updater Safes. Safe thresholds, owners, modules, guards, fallback handlers, and master copies were read onchain. The deployed BoringVault and LayerZeroTeller contracts are immutable non-proxy deployments. The native deposit() path enters each chain's collateral-gated BoringVault share accounting; the same LayerZeroTeller's cross-chain vault.exit()/zero-asset vault.enter() path is separately scored under Bridge Risk and is not a native unbounded-mint observation. Reconciliation review (2026-08-08): deposited stablecoins are locked 1:1 in an Ethereum Veda BoringVault and deployed only into on-chain lending and staking protocols, with the strategy whitelist explicitly limited to audited protocols above $100M TVL and backing addresses disclosed across three Ethereum and three Sonic vaults. The mint path creates no off-chain reserve claim, so reconciliation is not-applicable. The only third-party work is smart-contract auditing (Spearbit, 0xMacro, OpenZeppelin), and no regulator appears anywhere in the stack. Economic-posture fields reviewed 2026-08-16: bounded immutable vault-share issuance remains collateral-gated; the on-chain-only claim is not applicable to reserve reconciliation and has no regulator or attestor.",
